# The browser smoke's fixture domain: engram files, written in the shape
# Crystalline's own emitter writes them (an unindented YAML sequence for tags
# among other things). Prettier reformats that frontmatter, which would leave
# the fixture looking unlike every engram the product itself produces.
e2e/fixtures

# What a browser smoke leaves behind: Playwright's own run record, traces and
# screenshots. Not ours to format, and a local smoke run would otherwise make
# the next format check fail on a file nobody wrote.
test-results
playwright-report

# The station game's golden rooms: the generator's own JSON.stringify output,
# pinned byte for byte by the tests. Prettier would pull short arrays onto one
# line and a golden would stop being what the generator writes.
src/game/world/golden/

# Clipboard samples for rich paste, in the shape other apps write them. A real
# capture replaces a file as it is, so prettier must not reshape them.
src/editor/fixtures/paste/

# Engram bodies whose tables the cell editor's fidelity test types into. They
# keep the spellings people write (no padding, no edge pipes, empty cells),
# which prettier would pad into one aligned shape.
src/editor/fixtures/tables/

# The hidden-mark fidelity test's dialect file: every Markdown spelling the
# editor draws (`*` and `+` bullets, `___` emphasis, setext headings, tilde
# fences), which prettier would rewrite into one style.
src/editor/fixtures/dialect/
